   :note "Earlier #2 (P1) and #20 (P2). The helper verifies directory ancestry, socket permissions and peer UID. Removal checks service stop, saved-state parsing, restoration, deletion and final state. Verification used a fake helper and unprivileged filesystem fixtures. Production launchd installation, system limit changes and privileged removal remain unverified.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-model-reference" :type :task :title "Validate GGUF extents, vocabulary and reference tokens" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/gguf.rs" "src/engine.rs" "src/main.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #3 and #4 (both P1). Checked tensor extents and vocabulary/logits dimensions guard model reads. The reference reader and shared setter verify token IDs and destination capacity before writing. Broader model loader findings have independent roadmap entries.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-agreement" :type :task :title "Require finite KL and full reference position counts" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/main.rs" "src/sampler.rs" "tests/ci.sh" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #5 (P1). The checker rejects nonfinite comparisons and the agreement gate requires all 58 short-decode, 24 long-prefill and 58 batched-decode positions. Historical M5 Pro agreement and the matching golden were measured on fb580e1. Earlier #15 (P2) remains partially open in the separate inference item for GPU sampling of nonfinite rows. CPU sampling rejects invalid rows.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-bind-framing" :type :task :title "Reject unusable keys and bound HTTP framing" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/main.rs" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #6 (P1) and #11 (P2). The parser requires values, rejects unusable configured keys, and requires explicit opt-in for an unkeyed resolved off-loopback address. Chunk frames and trailers have length bounds and bodyless routes dispatch after headers. The non-loopback safeguard is implemented in main at be82ef3.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-decode-status-shape" :type :task :title "Check Metal completion and supported decode shapes" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/engine.rs" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #7 and #8 (P2). The scheduler checks command completion before consuming prefill or decode outputs. Startup validates the effective lane count, pipeline and allocated decode arena. Device failure and shape checks from the morning repair used fb580e1.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-cancellation-output" :type :task :title "Release cancelled work and bound stalled output" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/serve.rs" "tests/servecheck/jobs.go" "tests/servecheck/gate.go" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #9, #10 and #16 (P2). Queued jobs retain their admission permits until disposal. Chat and Messages poll disconnected clients during hidden thinking. Each lane has bounded output buffering, and stalled socket writes time out.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-budget-encoding" :type :task :title "Validate token budgets and continue after damaged UTF-8" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/serve.rs" "tests/servecheck/validation.go" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #12, #13 and #14 (P2). Messages clamps positive budgets to available reply space. Chat validates both budget names and rejects invalid supplied values before admission. Both stream handlers replace damaged UTF-8 and flush incomplete tails.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-preprocess" :type :task :title "Bound preprocessing before prompt rendering" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/serve.rs" "src/tokenizer.rs" "docs/LANE-SWEEP.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #17 (P2). Generation checks admission and limits tokenization before accepting the full prompt. Concurrent preprocessing is bounded at the greater of four and the effective lane count. The operating guide still describes the morning four-request limit.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-preprocess-guide" :type :task :title "Document the lane-dependent preprocessing limit" :state :doing
   :evidence ("docs/README.md" "docs/LANE-SWEEP.md" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/91")
   :note "Reconciliation caveat for earlier #17. Update the operating guide and cover a lane count above four so the implementation's concurrency bound and its documented behavior agree.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-soak-load" :type :task :title "Require successful streamed workloads and valid load rates" :state :done
   :evidence ("tests/soak_client.go" "tests/soak_client_test.go" "tools/load/main.go" "tools/load/main_test.go" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #18 (P2) and #23 (P3). Soak validates completion events, successful representative work and recovery. The load client measures per-stream throughput from elapsed time as needed and fails incomplete runs. Spill qualification and telemetry have separate findings.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-cli-context" :type :task :title "Enforce supported context sizes and correct CLI turn accounting" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/main.rs" "src/session.rs" "tests/ci.sh" "docs/README.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/63")
   :note "Earlier #19 (P2), #21 and #22 (P3). The parser enforces a rounded maximum of 262,080. Interactive chat preserves the first turn after oversize input, and zero-token generation returns before sampling or emitting a token.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-memd-lease" :type :task :title "Reacquire the memory reservation after the helper restarts" :state :doing
   :evidence ("src/memd.rs" "src/main.rs" "tests/soak_faults.sh" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/84")
   :note "A surviving server can lose its wired-memory reservation when the daemon restores the saved limit. Local repair f89d3f5 keeps an owned lease, detects disconnection and reconnects. The same fake-helper restart check failed on 7a27806 and passed after the repair. The binary test suite passed 229 tests with seven ignored, and the separate CLI restart integration test passed. Merge and privileged production qualification are outstanding.")
  (:id "t-audit-prior-window-oracle" :type :task :title "Isolate the retained-window cold reference from the warm cache" :state :doing
   :evidence ("tests/servecheck/main.go" "tests/servecheck/replies.go" "tests/servecheck/servecheck_test.go" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/84")
   :note "The follow-up used for the cold reference primes the same server that later checks reuse. Local c6bb259 uses separate fresh single-lane instances and verifies zero initial cached tokens, base-bounded warm reuse and identical replies. Eight focused cases, the full servecheck Go suite, vet and build passed on Linux. Merge and model-backed verification of the new setup are outstanding.")
