  (:id "t-audit-verify-package" :type :task :title "Verify the published v0.2.2 source and release assets" :state :done
   :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/releases/tag/v0.2.2" "Cargo.lock" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/be82ef36c93672c715312676d40c25e9dfeb6fff")
   :note "All 129 files in the public crate matched the rebuilt package byte for byte. The two GitHub release assets matched their published SHA-256 checksums. The OSV check of the 20 locked third-party packages returned no matching advisory on November 24, 2026.")
  (:id "t-audit-verify-compiled" :type :task :title "Run the released Rust and Go suites" :state :done
   :evidence ("Cargo.toml" "tests/go.mod" "tools/inkconvert/go.mod" "tools/load/go.mod" "tools/replay/go.mod" "tools/xsim/go.mod")
   :note "The locked Studio Rust suite passed 228 tests with seven ignored. On Linux all six packages with tests passed the race detector. All five Go modules built and passed vet. These results apply to v0.2.2.")
  (:id "t-audit-verify-hardware" :type :task :title "Verify M5 Max and Pro reference agreement and chip goldens" :state :done
   :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/actions/runs/45538544639/job/138951078907" "tests/ci.sh" "tests/golden.sh")
   :note "The tagged main revision matched llama.cpp at all 58 short-decode, 24 prefill and 58 batched-decode positions. On M5 Pro the corresponding worst KL divergences were 0.000001637, 0.006897324 and 0.000381056. Chip-specific goldens, lane and pool checks also passed.")
  (:id "t-audit-verify-http" :type :task :title "Check the published binary and the three-turn RAM cache on M5 Pro" :state :done
   :evidence ("tests/serve.sh" "tests/servecheck/main.go" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/releases/tag/v0.2.2")
   :note "The v0.2.2 release binary passed 17 loopback API checks. A separate paged-scheduler test matched 16 cold private-lane tokens on each of three turns, reusing 10,048 and 10,112 prompt tokens. SSD qualification has a separate row.")
  (:id "t-audit-verify-models" :type :task :title "Replay shipped model traces and their negative controls" :state :done
   :evidence ("scripts/check-tla.sh" "specs/README.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/be82ef36c93672c715312676d40c25e9dfeb6fff")
   :note "The v0.2.2 TLA runner accepted its positive traces and rejected the five MemMode, six blockbook, seven cache and four scheduler mutations. Its synthetic scheduler traces have separate coverage from the live planner.")
  (:id "t-audit-ci-unix-socket-path" :type :task :title "Run helper socket tests independently of checkout path length" :state :doing
   :evidence ("src/memd.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/84")
   :note "Two macOS helper tests exceeded the Unix socket pathname limit when run from a long checkout. Create a short, private scratch directory for each test and preserve isolation across concurrent runs.")
  (:id "t-audit-verify-umask-fixtures" :type :task :title "Isolate the helper socket test from concurrent recorder tests" :state :doing
   :evidence ("src/memd.rs" "src/record.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/91")
   :note "The helper socket test temporarily changes the process-wide file mask. In a parallel run a recorder fixture directory was created without search permission and rotation failed. Run the helper fixture in its own process and use a deterministic recorder write failure.")
  (:id "audit-serve" :type :roadmap :title "Rowan's audit: serving defects"
   :rows (
     ("au-conn-slots" "Each peer has a connection cap, and the entire request upload has a deadline ([#100](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/100))")
     ("au-count-tokens" "count_tokens limits request bytes and rendered tokens and uses its own preprocessing permit ([#100](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/100))")
     ("au-admit-scan-cost" "Admission checks shared prefixes in time linear in the prefilling lanes, with no all-pairs rescans while the GPU waits ([#112](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/112))")
     ("au-loopback-bind" "inky serve refuses a bind address that is neither loopback nor private, so the binding rule the server and fleet rows state holds ([#111](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111))")
     ("au-recorder-bytes" "The recorder queue is bounded in bytes and holds no copy of refused requests ([#111](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111))")
     ("au-fleet-record-optin" "The fleet script records card traffic only when asked, into a directory git ignores ([#109](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109))")
     ("au-pool-floor" "inky serve refuses to start when its K/V budget cannot hold one request at the pool's hard floor ([#111](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111))")
     ("au-memd-boot-tag" "The saved-limit record survives a clock step, so a helper restart always restores the limit it found ([#109](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109))")
     ("au-browser-origin" "An unkeyed loopback server checks Host, Origin and Content-Type, so a web page in a local browser cannot drive it ([#111](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111))")
     ("au-slow-stream" "A streaming client that reads too slowly is cut off by a total write deadline and frees its lane ([#111](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111))")
     ("au-accept-emfile" "The accept loop backs off and logs on errors, and the connection cap sits below the descriptor limit ([#109](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109))")
     ("au-evict-bounded" "An allocation that eviction cannot satisfy fails without emptying the cache, and a rolled-back span leaves the cache as it was ([#112](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/112))")
   )
   :columns (("done" "done"))
   :cells (
     ("au-conn-slots" "done" "t-au-conn-slots")
     ("au-count-tokens" "done" "t-au-count-tokens")
     ("au-admit-scan-cost" "done" "t-au-admit-scan-cost")
     ("au-loopback-bind" "done" "t-au-loopback-bind")
     ("au-recorder-bytes" "done" "t-au-recorder-bytes")
     ("au-fleet-record-optin" "done" "t-au-fleet-record-optin")
     ("au-pool-floor" "done" "t-au-pool-floor")
     ("au-memd-boot-tag" "done" "t-au-memd-boot-tag")
     ("au-browser-origin" "done" "t-au-browser-origin")
     ("au-slow-stream" "done" "t-au-slow-stream")
     ("au-accept-emfile" "done" "t-au-accept-emfile")
     ("au-evict-bounded" "done" "t-au-evict-bounded")
   ))
  (:id "t-au-conn-slots" :type :task :title "Each peer has a connection cap, and the entire request upload has a deadline" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/serve.rs: ConnectionSlots" "src/serve.rs: handle_connection" "src/serve.rs: connection_slots_enforce_peer_and_global_limits_and_reuse_released_slots" "src/serve.rs: partial_http_bodies_expire_within_the_request_read_deadline" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/100")
   :severity "high" :audit "U27"
   :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. An unkeyed peer can hold all 512 slots for 10 s each before auth (serve.rs:2619-2630) with no per-peer cap, and accept errors retry with no pause (serve.rs:2616). Findings: U27. The listener allows 128 live connections per canonical peer IP within the 512-connection global cap and backs off 100 ms after accept errors. From acceptance, the server allows 10 seconds for headers and 60 seconds for the entire upload. Tests cover both body framings and released slot reuse.")
  (:id "t-au-count-tokens" :type :task :title "count_tokens limits request bytes and rendered tokens and uses its own preprocessing permit" :state :done
   :evidence ("src/serve.rs: handle_connection" "src/serve.rs: count_tokens" "src/serve.rs: count_tokens_http_limits_both_body_framings_and_rendered_tokens" "src/serve.rs: count_tokens_uses_a_dedicated_http_preprocess_slot" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/100")
   :severity "high" :audit "U28"
   :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. count_tokens (src/serve.rs:2487) still tokenizes a 32 MiB single-run body with usize::MAX, so bpe_ranked allocates ~1.5 GiB per request while holding a shared preprocess permit (serve.rs:2486,2571). Findings: U28. The count route accepts up to 1 MiB of JSON in either framing and up to 262,144 rendered tokens. JSON decoding and rendering use one count-only permit. Loopback tests exercise both body limits, the rendered-token limit, and saturation of each processor pool while the other route remains available.")
  (:id "t-au-admit-scan-cost" :type :task :title "Admission checks shared prefixes in time linear in the prefilling lanes, with no all-pairs rescans while the GPU waits" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/a33b0bd1cb1fd5e2324d8a696b9aee65065930a5" "src/serve/block_cache.rs: compute_block_hashes, PreparedInflightCohort, can_admit_with_cohort" "src/serve/block_cache/admission_tests.rs" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/112") :severity "medium" :audit "U331" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. Each admission still runs all-pairs inflight_shared_checkpoint over prefilling lanes with full-prefix slice compares (block_cache.rs:180-209, 256-280, 484), cubic per burst on the scheduler thread. Findings: U331.")
  (:id "t-au-loopback-bind" :type :task :title "inky serve refuses a bind address that is neither loopback nor private, so the binding rule the server and fleet rows state holds" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/e07a9410980b50c7ba83dcf7e42ce6fc625413c6" "src/serve.rs: validate_bind_addrs" "src/main.rs: parse_serve" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111") :severity "medium" :audit "U48" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. No code restricts --bind to loopback/private ranges (src/main.rs:177-178); is_private_ip only picks a log string (src/serve.rs:2584), yet roadmap.sexp:819,854 and FLEET-SPRINT.md:3 claim it. Findings: U48.")
  (:id "t-au-recorder-bytes" :type :task :title "The recorder queue is bounded in bytes and holds no copy of refused requests" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/e07a9410980b50c7ba83dcf7e42ce6fc625413c6" "src/record.rs: Recorder::with_limits" "src/serve.rs: chat_with_card, messages_with_card" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111") :severity "medium" :audit "U22" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. Recorder queue is still bounded by count (record.rs:343, 1024 entries) and each entry deep-clones the request body (serve.rs:2072), including 400 refusals (serve.rs:2098). Findings: U22.")
  (:id "t-au-fleet-record-optin" :type :task :title "The fleet script records card traffic only when asked, into a directory git ignores" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/760247a45bb6c90abd8b30ba2905acebcc82cf76" "scripts/inky-fleet-serve.sh" "tests/fleet_serve_script.rs" ".gitignore" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109") :severity "medium" :audit "U53" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. scripts/inky-fleet-serve.sh:30,68 always records full card traffic into $REPO_ROOT/logs/cards, which .gitignore does not ignore; :57 hides chmod failure with // true. Findings: U53.")
  (:id "t-au-pool-floor" :type :task :title "inky serve refuses to start when its K/V budget cannot hold one request at the pool's hard floor" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/e07a9410980b50c7ba83dcf7e42ce6fc625413c6" "src/engine.rs: serve_pool_floor_counts, checked_serve_block_pool_counts, try_init_serve_block_pools" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111") :severity "medium" :audit "U72" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. serve still starts with a 1-window/1-full pool when KV budget is ~0 (engine.rs:961-971, serve.rs:1715-1724); requests over ~67 tokens are now refused as too long instead of pool-exhausted, but nothing refuses startup. Findings: U72.")
  (:id "t-au-memd-boot-tag" :type :task :title "The saved-limit record survives a clock step, so a helper restart always restores the limit it found" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/760247a45bb6c90abd8b30ba2905acebcc82cf76" "src/memd.rs" "specs/memmode/MemMode.tla" "specs/memmode/RestoreStale.cfg" "specs/memmode/StaleBoot.cfg" "scripts/memmode-traces.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109") :severity "medium" :audit "U81" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. The saved record is keyed on the exact kern.boottime second (src/memd.rs:131-134). After a clock step it is treated as StaleBoot and deleted without a restore (:312-315, :585), which leaves the limit raised. Findings: U81.")
  (:id "t-au-browser-origin" :type :task :title "An unkeyed loopback server checks Host, Origin and Content-Type, so a web page in a local browser cannot drive it" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/e07a9410980b50c7ba83dcf7e42ce6fc625413c6" "src/serve.rs: check_headers_with_policy" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111") :severity "medium" :audit "U94" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. Unkeyed loopback server never checks Host, Origin or Content-Type (serve.rs:1529-1548, 1608-1617, 2673-2684), so a browser text/plain POST or DNS-rebinding page can drive it. Findings: U94.")
  (:id "t-au-slow-stream" :type :task :title "A streaming client that reads too slowly is cut off by a total write deadline and frees its lane" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/e07a9410980b50c7ba83dcf7e42ce6fc625413c6" "src/serve.rs: StreamDeadlineWriter" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/111") :severity "medium" :audit "U96" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. The 5 s write timeout is per write call (src/serve.rs:1904, 2617), so a client draining just under every 5 s holds its lane until max_tokens. Findings: U96.")
  (:id "t-au-accept-emfile" :type :task :title "The accept loop backs off and logs on errors, and the connection cap sits below the descriptor limit" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/760247a45bb6c90abd8b30ba2905acebcc82cf76" "src/serve.rs" "src/memd.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/109") :severity "medium" :audit "U100" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. Accept loops at src/serve.rs:2615-2616 and src/memd.rs:428 still retry accept errors (EMFILE) immediately with no backoff or log; MAX_CONNS=512 (serve.rs:1902) exceeds the 256 default fd limit. Findings: U100.")
  (:id "t-au-evict-bounded" :type :task :title "An allocation that eviction cannot satisfy fails without emptying the cache, and a rolled-back span leaves the cache as it was" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/a33b0bd1cb1fd5e2324d8a696b9aee65065930a5" "src/serve/block_cache.rs: select_eviction_victims, ensure_span_blocks" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/112") :severity "medium" :audit "U105" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. take_zeroed_slot_inner (block_cache.rs:1194-1207) still evicts and spills every retained start before PoolExhausted; ensure_span_blocks rollback (:1241-1246) does not restore them. Findings: U105.")
  (:id "audit-models" :type :roadmap :title "Rowan's audit: models and trace checks"
   :rows (
     ("au-starttails-serve" "Replay ServeBlockCache start-point retention, window holds and pruning against the StartTails rules")
     ("au-prefixtree-serve" "Replay and mutate the EntryTree path used by serve, including handle refresh and pruning")
     ("au-serve-mutants" "The trace-gate mutants are planted in code inky serve computes with, and each turns its gate red ([#124](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/124))")
     ("au-window-rule" "The models keep the window rule the server prunes by, and the WindowOffByOne witness reports a real off-by-one ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-multiblock-span" "CacheScheduler models spans that cross block boundaries, as every production prefill chunk does ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-start-state" "CacheScheduler models a start point's recurrent state with its own tier and budget, so StartPointsKept can fail ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-decode-seal" "The model and the scheduler twin never seal decode-written blocks or keep start points on them, as decision 4 says ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-bypass-ghost" "BypassBoundHolds counts pass-overs with an independent ghost counter and is checked at a bypass bound above 1 ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-writeback-guard" "BuildStep waits for an in-flight cold writeback in the model as in the code, so the block keeps its I/O protection ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-spillable" "ColdBlocksSpillable states a spillability condition that a model which never spills would fail ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-inblock-kernels" "The in-block address arithmetic the Metal kernels run is bound to the InBlock model by trace or test ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-trace-actions" "Trace replay checks each step's named action and arguments, so a step that changes nothing is refused ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-engine-models" "The kv-disk tier, the sliding-window ring and prefill scratch, rollback_verify and VecAlloc each have a state or layout model ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-blockedslab-model" "BlockedSlab slot reuse, stride growth and the packed block-table upload have a layout model run at capacity 3 or 4 ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
     ("au-slab-word" "The slab-packed GPU block-table word has a layout model and a multi-slab test of packing, shader decode and bind order ([#114](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/114))")
   )
   :columns (("done" "done"))
   :cells (
     ("au-starttails-serve" "done" "t-au-starttails-serve")
