  (:id "t-au-doc-design-starts" :type :task :title "DESIGN.md and the roadmap state the start-point stride and step building the server runs, one policy the model and gates share" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/dff0447f031092447249d567ce0c11cde3d8d496" "docs/DESIGN.md" "docs/roadmap.sexp" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/113") :severity "medium" :audit "U44, U137" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. block_cache.rs:20-23,1339-1348 keep start points only every 2048/4096 tokens plus prompt ends, never at lane heads, while DESIGN.md:119 and done row roadmap.sexp:741 claim every 16 blocks and heads. Findings: U44, U137.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-design-status" :type :task :title "DESIGN.md's status line and layer table agree with the roadmap, and DSPARK.md cites current line numbers" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/dff0447f031092447249d567ce0c11cde3d8d496" "docs/DESIGN.md" "docs/DSPARK.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/113") :severity "low" :audit "U134, U135, U136" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. docs/DESIGN.md:3 still says Layer 3 is in progress and the server runs ahead of the block cache, while the roadmap marks the layer 3 rows done (ROADMAP.md:297, roadmap.sexp:741). Findings: U134, U135, U136.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-design-agree" :type :task :title "tests/ci.sh and DESIGN.md describe what the long-prompt agreement check compares" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/dff0447f031092447249d567ce0c11cde3d8d496" "tests/ci.sh" "docs/DESIGN.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/113") :severity "low" :audit "U314" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. tests/ci.sh:5 calls the long run a prefill check and docs/DESIGN.md:65 says the long decode path is unchecked, yet ci.sh:40 with INK_PF=2380 compares 23 decode-path rows of 24. Findings: U314.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-memd-sleep" :type :task :title "DESIGN.md, memd.rs and MemMode.tla say what the code does when the machine sleeps" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/f9f658595102daf364d84add6a89398f94255b2e" "docs/DESIGN.md" "src/memd.rs" "specs/memmode/MemMode.tla" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119") :severity "low" :audit "U239" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. src/memd.rs:4, specs/memmode/MemMode.tla:4 and docs/DESIGN.md:163 claim a sleep closes the connection; nothing closes it on sleep, so the limit stays raised. Findings: U239.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-readme-serving" :type :task :title "docs/README.md documents the engine environment variables that change serving" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/f9f658595102daf364d84add6a89398f94255b2e" "docs/README.md" "src/engine.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119") :severity "low" :audit "U205" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. INK_OLD_MIXB, INK_HEADROOM, INK_SPLITS, INK_POISON_RANGE, INK_DBATCH_A etc. read in src/engine.rs (1803, 1947, 2110, 3179, 3254) remain undocumented in docs/README.md:345. Findings: U205.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-roadmap-evidence" :type :task :title "Roadmap evidence names files and functions that exist on the path serve runs, and row states match the code" :state :done :evidence ("docs/roadmap.sexp" "docs/ROADMAP.md" "tests/servecheck/gate.go" "src/serve.rs" "src/serve/block_cache.rs" "src/engine.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/125") :severity "low" :audit "U144, U151, U152, U153" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. ROADMAP.md:436 lists GPU sampling as not done though serve.rs:1198 uses it; engine.rs:677,1093 dead_code 'wired after merge' and engine.rs:512,812,841 'pools unused' comments are stale. Findings: U144, U151, U152, U153.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-releases" :type :task :title "Release notes and the serve.rs header describe the cross-card reuse and lane states the code has" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/f9f658595102daf364d84add6a89398f94255b2e" "src/serve.rs" "docs/releases/v0.1.0.md" "docs/releases/v0.2.0.md" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119") :severity "low" :audit "U145, U146" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. serve.rs:4-10 header still describes the removed kept-prompt/copy_lane_prefix design instead of ServeBlockCache checkpoints in serve/block_cache.rs. Findings: U145, U146.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-loopcd" :type :task :title "LoopCD has a roadmap row, a design section and serve documentation" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/049ca079e342489855627b55a8671d1508df659b" "docs/DESIGN.md" "docs/README.md" "src/engine.rs" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/124") :severity "low" :audit "U147" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. docs/README.md has no --loopcd/loopcd_omega entry though v0.2.2.md:41 says it covers every serve flag (serve.rs:2127); no roadmap feature row for LoopCD. PR #86 fixes the README part only. Findings: U147.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-specs" :type :task :title "specs/README.md, RESULTS.md and CACHE_SCHEDULER.md describe the models and runs CI has, PrefixTree and the 429 rule included" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/4f17e8c3eb0c345697786eb385077ae7f08cbf49" "specs/README.md" "specs/RESULTS.md" "specs/CACHE_SCHEDULER.md" "specs/CacheScheduler.tla" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117") :severity "low" :audit "U60, U150, U160, U173, U174, U182, U183" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. specs/CacheScheduler.tla:301-304 and CACHE_SCHEDULER.md:44-53 claim queued requests are never 429-refused matching serve.rs, but src/serve.rs:1860-1864,1974 refuses queued waiters after 60 s. Findings: U60, U150, U160, U173, U174, U182, U183.")
  (:id "t-au-doc-code-comments" :type :task :title "Code comments in blocks.rs, prefix.rs, engine.rs, main.rs, poolgate.rs and serve.rs describe what is wired today" :state :done :evidence ("https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/commit/f9f658595102daf364d84add6a89398f94255b2e" "src/blocks.rs" "src/prefix.rs" "src/engine.rs" "src/main.rs" "src/poolgate.rs" "src/serve.rs" "https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119") :severity "low" :audit "U187, U202, U230, U253, U270" :note "Rowan Claude, 2026-11-25: audit of be82ef3, re-checked on main at 21966b0. Stale comments remain at blocks.rs:252 (fp16 stride), prefix.rs:20 (LiveTree) and main.rs:958 (candidate is layer 2), and Layer2::candidate_label (poolgate.rs:301) is still dead. Findings: U187, U202, U230, U253, U270.")
  (:id "audit-small" :type :roadmap :title "Rowan's audit: smaller defects"
   :rows (
     ("au-s-release" "Release tags are protected, the crates.io publish fails loudly without its token, and the token is scoped to release tags ([#123](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/123))")
     ("au-s-branches" "Merged branches are deleted, open fix branches land or close, and no run on main is cancelled without a verdict")
     ("au-s-ci-pins" "Every workflow pins actions by SHA and the Rust toolchain by version, and builds with --locked ([#113](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/113))")
     ("au-s-ci-zero-tests" "CI test steps fail on zero matched tests, and every ignored test runs in a tier or is ledgered ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-runner-wait" "A job with no M5 runner online fails with a message instead of waiting in the queue ([#123](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/123))")
     ("au-s-fleet-scripts" "The fleet script's lane, effort and queue defaults are the ones the lane sweep measured ([#91](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/91))")
     ("au-s-public-hygiene" "The public repository holds no host inventory, network addresses, firewall state, account paths or secret-store layout ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-tunings" "The default tuning budget cannot underflow on a small or unreadable memory size ([#91](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/91), [#118](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/118))")
     ("au-s-poisongate-model" "PoisonGate.tla is bound by trace to poolgate, with take, share and release inside the poisoned phase ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-scheduler-walk" "The scheduler twin's walks assert drain, reach the disk tier and check invariants, and cancel during restore is modelled ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-mutant-pinning" "Trace checkers pin each mutant to the property it names and require every action, spill and restore to appear ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-blocklayout-invariants" "BlockLayout and SpanPins invariants can fail in a healthy run, and each has a witness ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-spec-bounds" "Model bounds hold two blocks, two window slots and two live start points, so the rules they check are exercised ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-witnesses" "Every checked property, MemMode liveness included, has a reversed witness that reports that property ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-cachescheduler-props" "CacheScheduler bounds, invariants and action properties can each fail, and least-recently-used order is visible to the trace ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-prefixtree-bounds" "PrefixTree's bounds tell Full from Window and deepest from shallowest, and its trace cannot pass by its seed alone ([#124](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/124))")
     ("au-s-trace-parse" "The cache trace walk and parser fail on any error or missing field ([#117](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/117))")
     ("au-s-prefill-zero" "Layer 2 prefill zeroes only its scratch and runs the output-matrix pass only for spans whose logits are read ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-model-load" "Model loading checks tokenizer fields, tensors and UTF-8 before GPU setup, and a changed file cannot alter a running server ([#113](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/113))")
     ("au-s-kv-disk" "--kv-disk is refused with --kv8, opens its file exclusively, checks snapshot fit, and has a bit-identical gate ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-engine-accessors" "Engine GPU-buffer accessors are bounds-checked or marked unsafe, and no slice outlives its borrow ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-loopcd" "LoopCD's weak-logits buffer is allocated up front and counted in the memory budget ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-engine-tests" "Engine tests check encode_spans_x, the shaders and the Metal argument structs themselves, not copies written in the tests ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-engine-input" "A step refuses spans that name the same lane twice, and INK_SPLITS=0 is refused ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-math-mode" "Shaders compile in a math mode that keeps the infinities and rounding the exactness claims rely on ([#123](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/123))")
     ("au-s-host-work" "Per-step host work in the block cache stays flat: no path copies at each start point and no CPU zero-fill of every slot ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-stream-writes" "OpenAI streaming writes each event through a buffer in one send ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-kernels" "Metal kernels use a device-scope acquire in last_tg, dead kernels are gone, and k_attn_b is split-invariant on window layers ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-shader-test" "The shader compile test fails when it compiles nothing, compiles every variant, and stays in its working directory ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-dead-code" "Dead serve and engine code is gone: kept-prompt lane choice, cross-lane copy and its xcopy gate, stale dead_code marks ([#124](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/124))")
     ("au-s-dead-mirrors" "Dead mirrors in blocks.rs, poolgate.rs and cache_scheduler.rs are gone or use the layouts the GPU uses ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-sampling" "The CPU sampler truncates to top_k without sorting the whole candidate set ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-cli" "CLI flags are validated, --seed 0 is a seed, long prompts are refused, unknown subcommands fail, and the renderer keeps text after bad UTF-8 ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-serve-startup" "inky serve reports a bad model file or bind address as an error before entering inky mode, and binds every resolved address ([#118](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/118))")
     ("au-s-request-fields" "Chat and Messages refuse wrongly typed fields and unrenderable content alike, and their errors state the real limits ([#118](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/118))")
     ("au-s-render-parse" "Error tool results tokenize whole, a generated role marker ends the reply, and streaming and non-streaming parse agree ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-http-framing" "Chunked bodies under the cap are accepted, and framing errors get a response sent after the body is drained ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-disconnect" "Disconnect detection handles half-close and bytes sent after the body ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-admission-gate" "The admission gate is tested with many waiters and probes sockets outside its lock ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-stream-keepalive" "Chat and Messages streams send keep-alives during prefill, hidden thinking and buffered tool calls ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-scheduler-health" "Scheduler-thread waits on the GPU and on spill writes have deadlines, and /health reports a stuck scheduler ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-cache-sidechannel" "Cached-token counts and restore timing tell a client nothing about other clients' prompt prefixes ([#124](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/124))")
     ("au-s-pool-accounting" "Lane memory is counted once, retained host copies are budgeted, deferrals are counted, and only lanes that cannot progress fail ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-block-cache-edges" "A failed rebind leaves the lane consistent, and a start being spilled owns the disk blocks it reuses from the start ([#120](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/120))")
     ("au-s-serve-tests" "The production scheduler test runs in CI, the stream-poll assertion can fail, and the thinking budget is tested through the scheduler ([#123](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/123))")
     ("au-s-unit-test-rules" "memd and spill unit tests use no real sockets, wall-clock time or child processes ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-memd-conns" "The memd helper and its clients read with timeouts, the accept loop backs off on errors, and the client cap sits below the descriptor limit ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-memd-saved" "The helper never lowers a higher limit, survives an unparsable saved file, passes its refusal reason, and the model covers that path ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-recorder-files" "Recorder files are private, never opened through symlinks, and written a whole line at a time ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-recorder-turns" "Recorder turn indexes survive tracker eviction, and the test-only recorder helpers are gone ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-replay" "tools/replay and tools/load unit tests use no sockets or real time ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-inkconvert" "tools/inkconvert checks counts and dimensions, refuses a converted base, reports unmatched -q6-tensors, and never wraps a Q8_0 block ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-xsim" "The research scripts and the reference oracle refuse edge inputs instead of crashing ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-poolgate" "poolgate requires sharing, reuse and pruning, crosses the 1024 window, and its start-point half has a witness and never skips ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-soak" "Soak verdicts fail on 429s under capacity, measure leaks net of the model, and require disconnects to stop generation ([#123](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/123))")
     ("au-s-servecheck" "serve.sh's one-test check is anchored, and the concurrent tool-call probe checks that its four requests overlapped ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-agreement" "The agreement gate checks the out-of-repo reference against the committed tokens ([#116](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/116))")
     ("au-s-tokenizer" "The production tokenizer's pre-splitter and Unicode tables have tests against known pieces ([#119](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/119))")
     ("au-s-table-word" "A cleared GPU block-table entry is distinct from slot 1, and release builds validate every block of a span ([#115](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/115))")
     ("au-s-eval-evidence" "Each evaluation measurement row names the job or recorded run that produced it ([#125](https://github.com/robotgamedevelopers/inky/pull/125))")
   )
   :columns (("done" "done"))
